                    {
                        "sense_id": "d78d6ed7-31b3-31b3-b5fd-18429f90256e",
                        "entry_id": "8eb5c414-7991-3f23-9d9f-d08afc202165",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Confined at close quarters"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "495819a2-8471-4b07-ab59-f4e667809cc0",
                                "sense_id": "d78d6ed7-31b3-31b3-b5fd-18429f90256e",
                                "text": "He did not realise that there was nothing personal in this aloofness, except in so far as he personified a larger life, whose hopeful outlook stirred in more cabined natures an unacknowledged resentment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9edc0dea-b615-42da-a8af-21c6971d6241",
                                "sense_id": "d78d6ed7-31b3-31b3-b5fd-18429f90256e",
                                "text": "They feel themselves in a state of thraldom; they imagine that their souls are cooped and cabined in, unless they have some man, or some body of men, dependent on their mercy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "261c8aef-d787-4cfa-84ce-34a40be34643",
                                "sense_id": "d78d6ed7-31b3-31b3-b5fd-18429f90256e",
                                "text": "Then, if there comes a click in his internal time-clock, he may set out upon another quest--more cabined, cribbed, and confined than any member of a Cook's tourist party."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
